@startuml run-lifecycle
' UML sequence diagram only: participants, lifelines, sync and async messages,
' replies and notes, and no other diagram or UML element type. The order is the
' order `run` takes it in: nothing is started before the network it joins
' exists.
' Source of record for docs/diagrams/run-lifecycle.svg. Do not edit the SVG:
' render it with the pinned PlantUML image (docs/adopting.md).
' &#45;&#45; is a literal "--": PlantUML reads --text-- as strikeout.
title run: preflight, the class side, the jail, reap

actor "operator" as H
participant "agentjail\nrun" as C
participant "podman" as P
participant "gateway container\nclass, dual-homed" as G
participant "jail container\nuid 10000, --rm" as J

H -> C : agentjail run <profile> &#45;&#45; <agent command…>
C -> C : load, validate, run the blockers,\nresolve the class, compute the grant
C --> C : the class, or the refusal that stops the run
C -> P : image inspect <gateway tag>
P --> C : the image ID (the container starts by ID, never by tag)
C -> P : container and network list/remove for resources\nwhose owning pid is dead (never by profile prefix alone)
P --> C : what was removed, or an error that is not read
C -> P : network create &#45;&#45;internal &#45;&#45;disable-dns &#45;&#45;ipv6=false\n<profile>-<pid>-<class>
P --> C : the network, or the error that stops the run
C -> P : network create &#45;&#45;ipv6=false <profile>-<pid>-egress
P --> C : the network, or the error that stops the run
C -> P : network inspect <profile>-<pid>-<class>
P --> C : internal, one subnet, IPv4 only
note over C
  The same verification function doctor &#45;&#45;network calls. A network that
  changed under you fails before anything starts, and a refusal is not a
  warning.
end note
C -> P : run -d gateway on both networks\n&#45;&#45;grant <profile egress ∩ class allowlist>\n&#45;&#45;audit-dir <state>/audit/<class>
P --> C : started, or the error that stops the run
P ->> G : run detached on the class and egress networks,\nwith the class config and the grant
note right of G
  An empty grant is announced ("this jail has no route out"), not refused:
  the gateway is started with --grant "" and permits nothing. The audit
  directory is created and pruned to the newest 20 runs per class before the
  jail starts.
end note
C -> P : read the gateway's address on the class network
P --> C : the address, or the exit code it exited with (reported as its\nrefusal), or no address after 15s: the run is refused
C -> P : run &#45;&#45;rm &#45;&#45;interactive jail on the class network\n&#45;&#45;dns <gateway> &#45;&#45;dns-search . &#45;&#45;env HTTPS_PROXY/ALL_PROXY
P -> J : start the jail (PID 1 is tini) and wait
J -> G : CONNECT host:port, the jail has no other peer
G --> J : 200 Connection established,\nthen the tunnelled bytes
H ->> C : SIGINT, SIGTERM, SIGQUIT
C ->> P : forward each signal to podman, then wait
P ->> J : the signal reaches container PID 1,\ntini, which forwards it to the agent
note over J : grandchildren of the agent are not signalled:\ntini forwards to its direct child only
J --> P : exit code, or 128 + signal
P --> C : the same code
C -> P : remove the gateway, then the egress network,\nthen the class network, on every exit path
P --> C : removed, or the warning that is printed
C --> H : exit with the agent's own code
note over H, J
  Synchronous calls (->) carry their reply (-->); the bare ->> arrows are
  asynchronous by design: a signal is a notification, and a detached gateway is
  not waited for. The tunnelled bytes after the CONNECT reply are a stream, not
  a message, and are not drawn.
end note
@enduml
